# A terminal's scrollback has a bar over the pane's last column — never
# a column of the child's own, so the child's size never changes. At the
# live bottom it stays out of the way (a press on that column is the
# terminal's); with the pointer on the column it shows: the thumb drags
# the view through the history, a press on the track pages. The pane
# fills rows 2..37 at 120x40, its last column is 119.
command view.toggle_tree
ex term sh -c "seq 1 200; exec cat"
wait 500
expect screen contains "▌200 "
expect screen contains "▌166 "
hover 40 10
click 119 3
expect screen contains "▌200 "
hover 119 10
drag 119 37 119 2
expect screen contains "▌1 "
expect screen lacks "▌200 "
click 119 37
expect screen contains "▌36 "
expect screen lacks "▌1 "
